# Test code inherits the project .clang-tidy and relaxes a few checks that fight
# GoogleTest/GoogleMock idioms. All three still apply to the library under src/.
#
# cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes: a GoogleTest fixture
#   exposes its state as protected members so TEST_F bodies, which derive from the
#   fixture, can reach it. That is the framework's own idiom. (Also covers the
#   public data member of a hand-written fake.)
# bugprone-unchecked-optional-access: a test guards a dereference with
#   ASSERT_TRUE(opt.has_value()) before reading *opt, but clang-tidy cannot model
#   that a gtest ASSERT returns on failure, so it flags the guarded access.
# bugprone-random-generator-seed: a deterministic test seeds its engine with a
#   fixed constant on purpose, so the result is reproducible run to run. Production
#   code, which should seed from a real entropy source, still gets the check.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -bugprone-random-generator-seed
